  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Justice Reform in Malaysia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to continue the use of NGO expertise to support criminal justice reform in Malaysia. This will be a continuation to support Malaysia on the establishment of a national sentencing council and guidelines to improve the justice system and support the justice pathway from arrest to imprisonment. The programme will address the gaps identified in the last 12 months by delivering targeted interventions through, local and commonwealth expertise to support reform. All outputs aim to support our overall outcome for the establishment of a sentencing council and guidelines. Key baseline research has already taken place on this including extensive stakeholder mapping in government to push for progress in the next 12 months.</narrative>
  </description>
